WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:09.680
Narrator: Nazar is the owner
of The Restorer in Ukraine.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:12.218
He specializes in repairing and restoring

00:00:12.218 --> 00:00:15.140
furniture with damage and defects.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:18.475
This is a wood-veneer
table with an oak base.

00:00:18.475 --> 00:00:20.530
The owner forgot to blow out a candle,

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:22.813
and it burned through the veneered surface

00:00:22.813 --> 00:00:24.250
into the wood.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.980
This left a 30-centimeter-wide hole

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.965
that's about 3 to 4 millimeters deep.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.950
Before he can start any restoration work,

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.510
he cleans and removes

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.400
as much of the burned area as possible.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.975
He uses a small grinder

00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:43.490
to remove the blackened layers.

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:44.965
Then he uses a blade

00:00:44.965 --> 00:00:47.781
to carefully remove larger pieces.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:50.380
After a basic cleaning and degreasing,

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.790
he adds clear packaging
tape over the entire area

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.760
and trims around it.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.620
This leaves only the damaged area exposed

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.503
and the other areas protected by the tape.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.535
Then it's time to repair the hole.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.500
To do this, he's using a wood putty.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.090
This acts as a filler and hardener

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:15.565
and can easily be covered

00:01:15.565 --> 00:01:17.940
with toners, paints, and varnish,

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.810
which he'll use later on in the process.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:23.143
After drying for about 40 minutes,

00:01:23.143 --> 00:01:24.251
the putty hardens,

00:01:24.251 --> 00:01:27.351
and he can sand it to
create a level surface.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.085
He uses a cloth with a light solvent

00:01:31.085 --> 00:01:32.251
to clean the dust off

00:01:32.251 --> 00:01:35.390
before moving on to the next step.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:37.733
After that, the tape comes off.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:48.090
To start adding color back
into the repaired hole,

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:51.100
he uses a mix of tints and furniture wax

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.863
that he's color-matched
to the original wood tone.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.510
He starts around the perimeter

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:58.563
and works his way into the center.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.345
He's doing this using a nozzle

00:02:01.345 --> 00:02:03.061
and gas soldering iron.

00:02:03.061 --> 00:02:05.910
This melts the wax onto the damaged area.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.600
The wax helps to restore
and fill the color

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.115
of the wood veneer.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.650
He finishes this repair
by leveling the surface

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.263
with an abrasive restoration fiber.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:23.120
Once the burns are removed
and the hole is filled,

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.840
it's time to add the wood grain.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.620
Nazar does this by painting it

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.230
with a tinted alcohol-based toner.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:31.871
He paints it in by hand

00:02:31.871 --> 00:02:33.763
and uses a semi-matte varnish

00:02:33.763 --> 00:02:36.432
to lock everything in
and keep it protected

00:02:36.432 --> 00:02:39.021
from dirt and water in the future.

